<urn:epcglobal:cbv:bt:0860009999060:HARVEST-2026-0417> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/bizTransactionType> <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BTT-prodorder> .
_:b238_b0 <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-04-17T11:26:42-04:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ref.gs1.org/epcis/EPCISDocument> .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "  ObjectEvent, action=OBSERVE, bizStep=transporting, disposition=in_transit." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "  bizLocation = Location GLN of the field / growing area / aquaculture container (KDE)." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "  bizTransactionList = reference document type + number KDEs." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "  destinationList type=location = immediate subsequent recipient location KDE." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "  eventTime = date of harvesting KDE." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "  quantityList.epcClass = GS1 Digital Link of GTIN+Batch/Lot (commodity + variety KDE)." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "  quantityList.quantity + uom = quantity and unit of measure KDE." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "  readPoint = Location GLN of the farm where the food was harvested (KDE)." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "  sourceList type=owning_party = harvester business identity KDE (phone etc. ride in master data of the GLN)." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Event 1 = harvesting itself: ObjectEvent, action=ADD, bizStep=creating_class_instance, disposition=active." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Event 2 = transport to the immediate subsequent recipient:" .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Harvest CTE per GS1 US 'EPCIS Recommendations for FSMA 204 CTEs' R2.0, §2." .
_:b238_b0 <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "NO usfsma: extension fields ride inside the event; everything maps onto native EPCIS/GS1 fields." .
